## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Event ID 30045 in 3CX event log | DID stored with `+` prefix or provider sending different format | Re-enter the DID without `+` (Step 2) and verify the provider sends matching format |
| SMS arrives at 3CX but no agent notified | Queue chat not enabled OR no agents assigned to queue | Step 4 — enable Chat on the queue, add agents |
| Agent sends reply, customer doesn't receive | Wrong Provider URL OR API Key in 3CX SMS tab | Re-copy both from your provider's portal (Part B) into 3CX SMS tab (Part C) |
| 3CX shows "Authentication Error" from provider | API Key mismatch | Re-copy API Key exactly — case-sensitive, no leading/trailing whitespace |
| **Enable SMS** checkbox is greyed out | No DID added yet | Add a DID first (Step 2), then return to the SMS tab |
| SMS goes to the wrong queue | DID routing in 3CX is mapped to a different queue | Check **Admin → Call Queues** for which queue holds that DID |
| Agent reply never arrives | 3CX → provider connection blocked by firewall / proxy | Ensure 3CX can reach the Provider URL host over HTTPS (port 443) |
| Customer's number shows as "Unknown" in 3CX | 3CX contact-matching is on but no record exists | Either disable Caller-ID Number Matching, or import contacts |
| Conversation shows in chat but agent can't type a reply | Agent isn't a member of the queue OR queue is paused | Add agent to queue / unpause queue |

### Reading the 3CX event log

For any of the symptoms above, the 3CX **Admin → Event Log** is the authoritative source. Filter by Event ID `30045` (SMS routing failures) to find dropped messages and their reason codes.

