## FAQ

**Q: Does this guide require the LiveKit Dashboard?**
No — this is a 3CX ↔ SMS provider integration. The dashboard's voice AI agents play no role in this customer-to-3CX SMS chat flow. If you want a voice agent to *also* send SMS *into* the 3CX chat (e.g. to brief a sales rep mid-call), see the separate `threecx_messaging` agent tool in the dashboard's Agents → Tools tab — that's a different flow that complements this one.

**Q: Which SMS providers support 3CX's Generic SMS?**
Any provider that documents support for 3CX's Generic SMS Webhook protocol. Common ones include Tronic Cloud, Twilio, Telnyx, and other carriers offering programmable SMS. Check your provider's documentation or support team for "3CX Generic SMS" or "3CX SMS Webhook" support.

**Q: Can I have multiple DIDs on the same SMS trunk?**
Yes. Add a row in the **DID Numbers** tab for each. Routing per-DID is configured in the queue / extension settings — each DID can point to a different queue.

**Q: Does international SMS work?**
Depends on your provider's coverage. Verify with your SMS provider that the destination countries you need are supported on your account.

**Q: Can I send MMS / images via this flow?**
3CX's Generic SMS protocol is text-only. MMS isn't carried through this trunk regardless of provider.

**Q: Will the customer see "Sender: 3CX" or similar?**
No — the `from` on the customer's screen is your DID number, exactly as you entered it (with the `+` re-added by the provider). If your provider supports alphanumeric sender IDs and you've configured one, the sender may show your business name instead, but that's account-level config at the provider, not part of this trunk setup.

**Q: What's the difference between this SMS integration and the dashboard's `threecx_messaging` tool?**
- **This guide**: customer-initiated SMS conversations that arrive in 3CX as chat. The customer can SMS your business and an agent replies from 3CX.
- **`threecx_messaging` tool** (separate, in the dashboard agent's Tools tab): a voice AI agent injects an internal SMS *into* 3CX's chat as if from a customer, so a 3CX user gets a notification with details. Use it for AI-to-human handoffs (e.g. "the AI just took a booking from 0416 ___ — here's the summary").

---

If you hit something this guide doesn't cover, copy the relevant 3CX Event Log line (Event ID + reason text) and the time of the test SMS — that's enough for your provider's support team to diagnose in one round-trip.
